    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **60 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**. BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July, labelled `FY<YY>` after the calendar year it ends in \u2014 e.g. dates in July 2025\u2013June 2026 are `FY26`).\n\n**New file** \u2014 `mapper/FiscalYear.java`: the single source of the fiscal-year rules, offering `endYearOf(date)`, `labelOf(...)` (yields `FY<YY>`), and `elapsedSince(from, to)` (whole fiscal years between two dates).\n\n**Changes:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`) property to the Owner schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field), and updated the `membershipNumber` / `membershipPoints` descriptions to the fiscal-year basis.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 mapped `fiscalYear` from the owner's business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` via `FiscalYear.labelOf`.\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java` \u2014 the `-M<YY>` segment now uses the fiscal-year's last two digits instead of the calendar year, so it always agrees with the returned `fiscalYear` (verified by Cp14).\n- `mapper/Membership.java` \u2014 tenure points now require **more than one elapsed fiscal year** (`FiscalYear.elapsedSince > 1`) rather than a 365-day window; a new owner still has zero tenure, preserving the level-3 cap (Cp39/Cp40).\n\nSince the stored `registrationDate` is already business-day-adjusted at creation (`BuildOwner` \u2192 `BusinessDay.effective`), all fiscal-year derivations are correctly based on the adjusted date. The two new tests (Cp14, Cp48) pass, as do all existing tests including the tenure/points/membership ones.\n\nI chose the ending-year FY naming (FY26 = 1 Jul 2025\u201330 Jun 2026) and a strict `> 1 fiscal year` tenure threshold to mirror the original `> 365 days` (more than one window); the tests pin format and internal consistency but not the exact FY value or old-tenure threshold, so both are consistent throughout.",
